  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Skill Library",
      "text": "> **One installable bundle, 100 practical skills.** This is not 100 separate npm plugins; it is a\n> single skill provider with 100 focused checklists across coding, testing, security, data, DevOps,\n> product, writing, research, career, marketing, and operations."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add /home/lrf/dsh/products/dsh-skill-library\n```\n\nAsk for a skill by name, or let the router/agent discover it from the skill catalog.\n\nFull list: [skills/INDEX.md](skills/INDEX.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Design",
      "text": "- Each skill has `name`, `description`, `whenToUse`, a method, verification, and explicit boundaries.\n- Skills are checklists, not proof of correctness; no fabricated sources or results.\n- Structural tests validate 100 unique skills, frontmatter, body length, and provider resolution.\n- Behavioral quality varies by skill; spot-check before relying on one."
    },
    {
      "section": "Limits",
      "text": "- 100 skills ≠ 100 independent host tools or 100 deep domain agents.\n- No benchmark proves all 100 improve task outcomes.\n- No open-problem or security-certification claims.\n- This library is separate from the 17 host/tool plugins in the portfolio."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm test\n```"
    }
  ],
